      "id": "usgs-original-identity",
      "method": "Read Shapefiles/Geocentric/Dune_Field.shp from https://pubs.usgs.gov/of/2007/1158/Shapefiles.zip (60,597,152 bytes, Last-Modified 6 July 2007) with pyshp and compare with the Trek response record by record.",
      "result": "547 records in both, same order, same vertex count per record, largest vertex difference 0 degrees. The USGS .prj names the flattened Mars 2000 ellipsoid, but its FGDC metadata defines the centroid latitude field as aerocentric and the folder is 'Geocentric'."
    },
    {
      "id": "area-against-publication",
      "method": "Area of cells whose centre falls in a polygon (cos-latitude weighted, 3,396.19 km sphere) against the database's own sinusoidal area field and a planar polygon-area estimate.",
      "result": "Dune fields: 4,132 cells, 70,230 km2; Area_sinu_ sums to 69,750 km2 and the USGS abstract gives about 70,000 km2. Chloride: 676 cells, 15,632 km2 against 15,588 km2 of polygon area."
    },
    {
      "id": "features-below-one-cell",
